Validation happens only in `BuildOwner` via `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`. When the incoming JSON violates the generated DTO constraints (required fields, sizes, or the `telephone` pattern `^[0-9]*$`, name patterns, etc.), Spring raises `MethodArgumentNotValidException`, which OfficeFloor routes to `ValidationExceptionHandler` -> `400` ProblemDetail. There is currently no telephone normalization and no exactly-10-digits rule on the create path (the `^[0-9]{10}$` rule lives only on the `Owner` entity, which the create flow does not bean-validate), which is exactly the gap the two acceptance tests in `AcceptanceTest.java` target.

